course: dictionary
lesson: 2723
title: Dinosaur: a word with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dinosaur is one of a large group of reptiles that lived on Earth millions of years ago and died out. Some were huge and some were small. Read the words around the word to check which meaning fits.
explain: «Sauropods were long-necked plant-eating dinosaurs and the biggest animals ever to walk on land.» The words plant-eating and biggest give you clues: the sentence is about a kind of dinosaur that ate plants and was very large.
explain: Dinosaur can also mean a person or thing that is old-fashioned and no longer useful. You can tell which meaning is meant by the sentence around it. If it talks about bones, eggs or millions of years, it means the animal.
fact: A dinosaur is one of a large group of reptiles that lived on Earth millions of years ago and died out.
fact: Scientists learn about dinosaurs from fossils: bones, teeth, eggs and footprints found in rocks.
fact: «Diplodocus» was about 25 metres long, mostly neck and tail.
fact: «Tyrannosaurus rex» ate meat, and «Diplodocus» ate plants.
fact: Most scientists think birds are living relatives of dinosaurs.
exercise: «Diplodocus was a plant-eating dinosaur.» What did Diplodocus eat? | Insects | *Plants | Fish | Meat
exercise: «Sauropods were long-necked plant-eating dinosaurs and the biggest animals ever to walk on land.» Which word tells you about size? | land | ever | walk | *biggest
exercise: Scientists learn about dinosaurs from what? | *Fossils such as bones, teeth, eggs and footprints | Photographs taken by children | Living dinosaurs in zoos | Stories only
test: Which of these is a fossil? | *A dinosaur footprint found in rock | A cat sleeping on a sofa | A sandwich | A cloud in the sky
test: Someone calls an old phone that no longer works a dinosaur. What does dinosaur mean here? | A huge reptile that is alive today | *Old-fashioned and no longer useful | A small bird | A fast car
exam: In its first meaning, what is a dinosaur? | A type of fish | A kind of sloth | *A large reptile that lived millions of years ago and died out | A bird that lives today
